 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And, as a king mine vision,\nI have known the blood of all men's dying.\nO king of heaven! O god and divine,\nSee that God in man alone\nThrough heav'n's open door doth able\nSpeak to the ground and shake it down again!\nFain were I, my kingdom, king on heaven,\nThat where thy feet tread, I might cannot\nKeep my heart up in its desire\nBy thee more than by myself.\nWith me shall God in heaven go along\nTo bear me down from this earth again",
